Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:55:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Retire W32 readers before slot reuse and reselect after callbacks

SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Chen Zhexuan
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

A reader can outlive deletion while a pipe writer remains open. Keep its
context, events and detached descriptor until the thread has exited,
without blocking the main thread. Transfer descriptor closure before
requesting retirement, then reclaim it exactly once on the main thread.
An independent retirement request cannot be overwritten by late I/O.

Preserve downstream 0035's prompt idle completion notifications, but poll
again after its callback-capable status notification and redisplay. Old
read/write readiness must not be consumed against replacement owners.

